The non-inverting terminal is directly connected to a \(1\,\text{V}\) source. Hence, \[V_{+}=1\,\text{V}\] For an ideal op-amp operating with negative feedback, \[V_{-}=V_{+}=1\,\text{V}\] Applying KCL at the inverting terminal, \[\frac{V_{-}-1}{10\,\text{k}\Omega}
+
\frac{V_{-}-V_{o}}{100\,\text{k}\Omega}=0\] Substituting \(V_{-}=1\,\text{V}\), \[\frac{1-1}{10\,\text{k}\Omega}
+
\frac{1-V_{o}}{100\,\text{k}\Omega}=0\] \[1-V_{o}=0\] \[V_{o}=1\,\text{V}\] \[\boxed{\text{(d) }1\,\text{V}}\]

The open-loop transfer function is \[G(s)H(s)=\frac{1}{(s+1)^3}\] \[\angle G(j\omega)H(j\omega)
=-3\tan^{-1}\omega\] The phase crossover frequency is obtained from: \[-3\tan^{-1}\omega_{pc}=-180^\circ\] \[\omega_{pc}=\tan60^\circ=\sqrt{3}\] The magnitude at \(\omega_{pc}\) is: \(|G(j\omega_{pc})H(j\omega_{pc})|
=\dfrac{1}{(1+\omega_{pc}^2)^{3/2}}
=\dfrac{1}{(1+3)^{3/2}}
=\dfrac{1}{8}\) Therefore, the gain margin is: \[\mathrm{GM}
=\frac{1}{|G(j\omega_{pc})H(j\omega_{pc})|}
=\frac{1}{1/8}
=8\] \[\boxed{(B)\;8}\]
